{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 36, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**A Whirlwind Adventure in Japan**\n\nJapan dazzled me in just seven days, blending ancient traditions with futuristic energy. My journey began in **Tokyo**, where neon lights pulsed alongside historic shrines. The **Senso-ji Temple** in Asakusa offered serene contrasts to the bustling streets of **Shinjuku**, packed with towering skyscrapers and tiny ramen shops. A bullet train whisked me to **Kyoto**, where cherry blossoms framed the paths of **Arashiyama** and lantern-lit alleys of **Gion**. At **Fushimi Inari**, thousands of vermilion torii gates stretched up sacred mountains—magical at sunrise.\n\nIn **Osaka**, I devoured **takoyaki** from street vendors and marveled at the **Osaka Castle**’s golden spires. A quick stop in **Nara** introduced me to friendly deer and the towering **Todai-ji Temple** Buddha. Back in Tokyo, I squeezed in last-minute sights: teamLab Planets’ digital wonderland, a quiet moment at **Meiji Shrine**, and one final bite of matcha-flavored treats in **Ginza**.\n\nJapan’s precision in every detail—from bullet-train punctuality to Michelin-starred sushi—left me awestruck. But it was the small moments that lingered: sipping green tea in a Kyoto garden, watching geisha glide by in Kyoto’s backstreets, and the hum of a vending machine offering hot coffee at midnight. A country of contrasts, Japan’s soul lies in its ability to balance the old and the new—leaving travelers, like me, breathless and already dreaming of returning.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.07225250452756882}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.42479637265205383}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.0445331335067749}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -0.01628841459751129}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": -7.986703712958843e-05}, {"token": " Adventure", "logprob": -1.2543786764144897}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.0651196613907814}, {"token": " Japan", "l